Source: nexusos-branding
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Maintainer: NexusOS Maintainers <maintainers@nexusos.invalid>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               librsvg2-bin,
               optipng,
               fonts-inter,
               fonts-jetbrains-mono
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/thrinadsanjay/NexusOS
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/thrinadsanjay/NexusOS
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/thrinadsanjay/NexusOS.git
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: nexusos-branding
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: fastfetch
Description: NexusOS Engineering Edition identity and artwork
 Provides the NexusOS operating system identity and brand assets:
 .
  * /usr/lib/os-release identifying NexusOS (ID_LIKE=ubuntu); the Ubuntu
    original is kept via dpkg-divert and restored when the package is removed
  * NexusOS release metadata (/usr/lib/nexusos/release)
  * default hostname for installers (never applied to the running system)
  * terminal banner and ASCII logo, fastfetch configuration
  * logos, application icon and KDE wallpaper packages
 .
 Kernel identity, /etc/lsb-release and APT configuration are not modified.
